uccess","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"ST028\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that Rule 6c-11 covers ETFs organized as registered open-end management investment companies. It also lists unit-investment-trust ETFs as needing separate exemptive relief.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that leveraged and inverse ETFs 'can also rely on 6c-11; they are no longer categorically excluded' and 'must comply with applicable Rule 18f-4 requirements.'\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Says nontransparent/semitransparent active ETFs and ETF share classes need separate exemptive relief. It also notes the daily portfolio transparency condition. Master-feeder structures are omitted, so the bundle is substantive but incomplete.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"No central error: the answer does not exclude leveraged/inverse ETFs, does not treat UITs as covered, and does not claim nontransparent ETFs or share classes avoid separate relief. The ancillary statements on 18f-4 grandfathering and commodity pools are not materially false. Coverage is 2.5 of 3 because master-feeder is missing from point 3, so not every required minimum is met. The grade is therefore partial.\"}","ttft_ms":4732,"type":"result","duration_ms":7996,"uuid":"8a01028e-ba4d-49d6-a985-59816761f0c2","ttft_stream_ms":1710,"time_to_request_ms":48,"first_content_frame_ms":1710,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
